    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 25-layer dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: alternating SiO2 and Al2O3 starting with SiO2, total 25 finite coating layers. Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 267.5 nm center wavelength (SiO2 ~45 nm, Al2O3 ~67 nm based on typical UV indices). Apply optimization bounds of ±8 nm from nominal for all layers. Include soft penalty term proportional to variance of adjacent Al2O3 layer thicknesses. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with learning rate reduced to 50% of default value. Evaluate coherent TMM transmission across three bands: 255-280 nm (maximize), 300-700 nm (minimize), 700-1100 nm (minimize). No metal layers permitted. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
